The page /vulnerabilities/xss_d/ contains client-side JavaScript that reads the 'default' parameter from document.location.href and writes it directly to the DOM via document.write() without sanitization.

Vulnerable code (from page source):
```
<script>
    if (document.location.href.indexOf("default=") >= 0) {
        var lang = document.location.href.substring(document.location.href.indexOf("default=")+8);
        document.write("<option value='" + lang + "'>" + decodeURI(lang) + "</option>");
        document.write("<option value='' disabled='disabled'>----</option>");
    }

    document.write("<option value='English'>English</option>");
    ...
</script>
```

The `lang` variable contains the raw URL substring after `default=` and is written directly to the value attribute without HTML encoding. An attacker can break out of the attribute and inject arbitrary HTML/JS.

PHP source (low level): `# No protections, anything goes`

Attack URL: /vulnerabilities/xss_d/?default=English</option></select><script>alert(document.cookie)</script>
